  "findings": [
    "Both normal-boot ELFs lack .debug_* DWARF sections and retain .symtab/.strtab. This is not merely a DWARF difference.",
    "Five of six PT_LOAD hashes differ; .text is 928 bytes smaller and .rodata is 7520 bytes smaller. Removing debug/symbol sections alone cannot make loaded images equal.",
    "Each .rodata embeds 931 occurrences of its checkout root (55 vs 47 bytes), plus 31 Rustup-root and 61 Cargo-root occurrences. This proves path dependence in runtime-loaded data.",
    "Runtime kernel/OSTD/dependency trees, key manifests/locks and compiler/LLD comments match. No controlled rebuild isolated the cause of every changed byte.",
    "The component macro emits absolute Cargo package paths as ordinary string literals; compiler source remapping does not rewrite these arbitrary literals."
  ],
  "config_remedy": {
    "a01_partial_remap_entry": "If separately authorized, render already-expanded --remap-path-prefix arguments into the owned generated minimal OSDK manifest [build].rustflags. It inherits into run/test. No core/SDK edit proposed.",
    "environment_only_limit": "cli.rs appends environment RUSTFLAGS to config.build after Config::new, while run/test do_cached_build reads config.run.build/config.test.build.",
    "toml_variable_limit": "canonicalize_and_eval evaluates only qemu.args; build.rustflags is a plain String. ${VAR} is not expanded.",
    "full_path_identity_constraint": "Use an explicitly fixed canonical absolute workspace and dependency/tool locations, or coordinate the component-literal issue with the core owner. A symlink alias alone is insufficient evidence.",
    "next_crosspath_proof": "After root same-host/path two-clean-target builds, compare a controlled two-checkout clean-target pair with identical pinned source/tools/dependencies/environment and explicit remap. Compare effective config, PT_LOAD hashes and absolute-root counts. Measure remaining component literals; do not assume whole-ELF equality."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Concrete path dependence is established; attributing every changed byte to checkout location is not established.",
    "OSDK host implementation changed between source receipts although runtime trees and kernel compile function/build manifest match. Environment logs do not retain all effective rustc argv.",
    "Historical debug-profile evidence retained a stripped boot ELF but not its 111867352-byte DWARF symbol ELF. No reconstructed symbol comparison or debug-to-normal equivalence is claimed.",
    "No cross-host, cold-build, component-order, username/hostname, or full crosspath determinism proof was performed."
  ]
